Hey folk,

I'm running a common factor GWAS and I am getting this error for one of the SNPs that is causing the program to crash:

Error in solve.default(t(S2.delt) %*% S2.W %*% S2.delt, tol = toler) :

  system is computationally singular: reciprocal condition number = 1.4036e-34

I've run CF GWAS several times for various models and this is the first time I've come across this issue.

To me the easiest solution would be just to skip these SNPs. I'm curious if other Users have seen this error. Any suggestions from the authors?

Hasuni

